WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:11.934
We just discussed private IP addresses, which are reserved address ranges for local use. Here is one more set of IP addresses not used publicly: any address starting with 127.

00:11.934 --> 00:25.756
To demonstrate, from a command prompt I will type, ping 127.0.0.1, and press Enter. I just pinged my own network card to see if it is working.

00:25.756 --> 00:34.823
I got a response, so the network card is working. This means that any network connectivity issues will not be a result of a bad network card.

00:34.823 --> 00:46.152
Here is one more address range for you: 169.254. This is known as APIPA, or Automatic Private IP Addressing.

00:46.152 --> 00:53.983
This is used when a device cannot get an IP address through a DHCP server, which is a server that gives out IP addresses to devices.

00:53.983 --> 01:01.294
DHCP will be covered in a little more detail later, but understand that if you see an IP address in this range,

01:01.294 --> 01:15.243
it means that the device cannot get an IP address from a DHCP server and thus can't connect to any devices except those in the same 169.254 address range.

